      "Red and amber only for states that need action.",
      "One sans (Inter), tabular numerals."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Accent Rule",
        "body": "Green is the only action colour. Letter colours never mean click here.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Identity Not Action Rule",
        "body": "Section colours say whose (which child, which section). They never mean do this; actions stay green.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Earned Alarm Rule",
        "body": "Red and amber appear only where they carry a state a person must act on.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Money Rule",
        "body": "Every amount and count uses tabular-nums. Colones written ₡185 000.",
        "section": "typography"
